Patch 17: 480fa1e04c47 — "io_uring: lift REQ_F_IOPOLL set out of issue path"
================================================================================

This patch moves the setting of REQ_F_IOPOLL from io_issue_sqe() (where it used
to be set per-op based on def->iopoll) up into io_init_req() so it happens before
submit_bio.

Why: registered slot IOs need REQ_F_IOPOLL set on the request before the bio is
submitted. The IOPOLL completion path must be selected at submission time, not
after. The slot's pre-allocated kiocb (slot->req) has REQ_F_IOPOLL set directly
at allocation time. For the ->prep handler to set it, the flag must already be
available on the request.

The commit also renames io_init_req to do_init_req because it becomes a helper
called from a new io_init_req wrapper that handles the allocation + init. The
new io_init_req additionally does the IOPOLL flag setting:

  static int io_init_req(struct io_ring_ctx *ctx, struct io_kiocb *req,
                         const struct io_uring_sqe *sqe, unsigned int *left)
          __must_hold(&ctx->uring_lock)
  {
          ...

          if (def->iopoll) {
                  req->flags |= REQ_F_IOPOLL;
                  ...
          }
          ...
  }

Previously this was in io_issue_sqe:

  static int io_issue_sqe(struct io_kiocb *req, unsigned int issue_flags)
  {
          ...
          if (def->iopoll)
                  req->flags |= REQ_F_IOPOLL;
          ...
  }

The diff also showed a timer_shutdown_sync pinning pattern — the author first
stashed an integer in a variable, then did the actual timer_shutdown_sync call,
and the variable is used after the call (keeps it alive via referencing).

