Patch 15: ff4208c36eef — "io_uring: factor out io_imu_offset_to_bvec() helper"
================================================================================

Extracts the offset-to-bvec lookup from the existing registered-buffer read/write
path into a reusable helper. The helper io_imu_offset_to_bvec() is defined as:

  bool io_imu_offset_to_bvec(struct io_mapped_ubuf *imu, loff_t offset,
                             struct bio_vec *bvec, unsigned long *b_off)

This answers: "given a byte offset within a registered buffer (struct
io_mapped_ubuf), which page (bvec) does it land on, and what's the offset
within that page?"

The struct io_mapped_ubuf represents a pre-registered buffer ring. It has
nr_bvecs entries, each describing a physically-contiguous chunk. All bvecs
have the same folio_shift (enforced at registration time by io_provide_buffers
or the buffer ring registration code — it rejects mixed folio sizes).

The helper is a page-table walk: it divides the offset by the folio size to
find the right bvec index, subtracts the prior bvecs' total size, and returns
the page pointer + offset within it.

Used by slot.c to translate the bio byte offset into a DMA-able page for the
persistent DMA mapping. Without this, the slot code would need to duplicate
the registered-buffer page-walk logic.

