Patch 11: 4ac8d063ed14 — "io_uring: support partitions for registered buffers"
================================================================================

When a registered slot targets a partition (e.g., /dev/nvme0n1p3), the IO
submitted via submit_bio_noacct_fast must target the correct sector on the
physical device. Partition block devices have bd_start_sect > 0.

The fix is to use bdev->bd_start_sect when computing bi_sector:

  slot->bio.bi_iter.bi_sector = (offset >> SECTOR_SHIFT) + bdev->bd_start_sect;

Without this, the IO would be submitted against sector 0 of the physical
device (the partition table area) instead of the partition's data area.

The commit message notes that the block device file's ->f_mapping tells us
about the partition offset. The bdev is obtained from the file's
->f_path.dentry->d_inode->i_bdev.

