Patch 8: 649b358554ed — "io_uring/slot: share persistent DMA mappings"
================================================================================

Deduplicates DMA mappings: if two slots use the same (buffer, device) pair,
they share a single persistent DMA mapping instead of each creating their own.

The sharing works via a cache on struct io_mapped_ubuf:

  struct io_mapped_ubuf {
      ...
      struct list_head dma_mappings;   // list of struct io_buf_dma
  };

io_buf_get_dma(imu, dev):
  - Walk imu->dma_mappings looking for an entry with matching dma_dev
  - If found: refcount_inc(&bd->refs), return &bd->dma
  - If not: create new mapping, add to list, return &bd->dma

io_buf_put_dma(imu, dma):
  - bd = container_of(dma, struct io_buf_dma, dma)
  - if (refcount_dec_and_test(&bd->refs)):
      - Call dma->driver_priv_destroy(dma) if set (NVMe PRP list teardown)
      - io_imu_dma_unmap(imu, dma)
      - list_del(&bd->list)
      - kfree(bd)

This matters because a single registered buffer can back multiple slots (same
buffer ring, different offsets), and they all target the same device. Without
sharing, each slot would do its own dma_map_sg / dma_map_page calls for the
same pages — wasting IOMMU resources and memory for seg_addrs arrays.

