Patch 6: 5d179cbf21b3 — "block: add RQF_REGISTERED flag"
================================================================================

Adds RQF_REGISTERED to the request flags and propagates BIO_REGISTERED from
the bio to the request at bio→request conversion time.

In enum rq_flag_bits (include/linux/blkdev.h or blk-mq.h):

  RQF_REGISTERED = (__force req_flags_t)(1 << 25),
  /* originates from a registered IO slot */

The propagation happens in blk_mq_bio_to_request() which is called during
bio submission:

  if (bio->bi_opf & REQ_BIO_REGISTERED)
      req->rq_flags |= RQF_REGISTERED;

Why is this needed? During completion, the driver needs to know whether this
IO came from a registered slot (to skip dma_unmap). By the time the request
completes, the bio may already be freed. Having the flag on the request avoids
needing to walk back to the bio.

The flag is also used by nvme_unmap_data() and nvme_complete_batch() to skip
the DMA unmap for registered IOs (see patch 5).

When the registered fast path falls back (BLK_STS_AGAIN), nvme_map_data()
clears RQF_REGISTERED so the completion path does the normal unmap:

  req->rq_flags &= ~RQF_REGISTERED;

