Patch 3: bc95526a1bb1 — "block: add ->persistent_dma_setup() hook"
================================================================================

Tiny patch — adds a driver callback hook to struct request_queue:

  struct request_queue {
      ...
      struct device *dma_dev;    // (from patch 5 setup)

      int (*persistent_dma_setup)(struct request_queue *q,
                                  struct io_slot_dma *dma);
      ...
  };

This is the block-layer contract point. When a persistent DMA mapping is
created for a given request_queue, the block layer calls this hook so the
driver can build its own private data structures.

The hook is called from io_buf_get_dma() (in patch 2):

  if (q->persistent_dma_setup)
      q->persistent_dma_setup(q, &bd->dma);

For NVMe, this hook is implemented by nvme_pci_persistent_dma_setup() (patch 1),
which builds a precomputed PRP list.

The hook receives struct io_slot_dma * (the persistent DMA mapping) and
returns 0 on success or a negative errno. If the setup fails, the entire
slot registration fails.

Note the reverse dependency: the callback takes struct io_slot_dma *, which
is defined in io_uring_types.h. This means the block layer header must either
include io_uring_types.h or forward-declare struct io_slot_dma. In the
original, it uses a forward declaration.

