Patch 2: 2e9c06025d7e — "io_uring/slot: add support for persistent driver DMA mappings"
================================================================================

Adds driver-private storage to struct io_slot_dma and wires up the
persistent_dma_setup callback.

New fields on struct io_slot_dma:

  struct io_slot_dma {
      ...
      void  *driver_priv;                // driver-specific data
      void  (*driver_priv_destroy)(struct io_slot_dma *dma);  // destructor
  };

driver_priv: The driver stores its private data here. For NVMe, this is
struct nvme_pci_persistent_prp * (the precomputed PRP list).

driver_priv_destroy: Called when the DMA mapping is being torn down (refcount
hits 0), so the driver can free its private data. For NVMe, this is
nvme_pci_persistent_dma_destroy() which does dma_free_coherent() for each
PRP list page.

The patch also changes io_buf_get_dma() to take struct request_queue * instead
of struct device *:

  // Before:
  slot->dma = io_buf_get_dma(imu, bdev_get_queue(bdev)->dma_dev);

  // After:
  slot->dma = io_buf_get_dma(imu, bdev_get_queue(bdev));

This is because io_buf_get_dma() now needs both:
  - q->dma_dev (the device for dma_map/dma_unmap)
  - q->persistent_dma_setup (the driver setup hook)

The call to q->persistent_dma_setup is added in io_buf_get_dma() after
the DMA mapping is created:

  static struct io_slot_dma *io_buf_get_dma(struct io_mapped_ubuf *imu,
                                            struct request_queue *q)
  {
      struct device *dma_dev = q->dma_dev;
      struct io_buf_dma *bd;
      int ret;

      // ... walk imu->dma_mappings for existing mapping ...

      // Create new mapping
      ret = io_imu_dma_map(imu, &bd->dma, dma_dev, dir);
      if (ret)
          goto err;

      // Driver setup hook
      if (q->persistent_dma_setup) {
          ret = q->persistent_dma_setup(q, &bd->dma);
          if (ret) {
              io_imu_dma_unmap(imu, &bd->dma);
              goto err;
          }
      }

      // ...
  }

And in io_buf_put_dma(), the destructor is called before unmapping:

  static void io_buf_put_dma(struct io_mapped_ubuf *imu, struct io_slot_dma *dma)
  {
      struct io_buf_dma *bd = container_of(dma, struct io_buf_dma, dma);

      if (!refcount_dec_and_test(&bd->refs))
          return;

      list_del(&bd->list);
      if (dma->driver_priv_destroy)
          dma->driver_priv_destroy(dma);      // free driver priv data
      io_imu_dma_unmap(imu, &bd->dma);       // unmap DMA
      kfree(bd);
  }

